# Line-ending policy.
#
# This repo is worked on from Windows paths under WSL, where an editor
# writing CRLF into a shell script is silently fatal: the kernel reads the
# shebang as "/bin/bash\r" and reports "bad interpreter". deploy.sh shipped
# broken that way until 2026-08-13. Pin the executable formats to LF so the
# checkout cannot reintroduce it, whatever core.autocrlf is set to locally.

*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

# Data and vocabularies are read by Python, which is newline-agnostic, but
# keeping them LF stops a checkout from rewriting every line of a 1.4 MB
# JSONL file and producing a diff with no content change.
*.jsonl text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf

# Never touch binaries or the source spreadsheets.
*.xlsx binary
*.pptx binary
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
